<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pōkarekare Ana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">probably about <a href="/years/1914">1914</a>; published <a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Pōkarekare Ana&quot; is a traditional <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> love song in the Māori language, probably composed communally about the time the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> began in 1914. Its author is not known.</p></div>
